  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Prevention, Protection and Governance in the Response to Human Trafficking in Ecuador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen prevention, protection, and governance in Ecuador&#x2019;s response to human trafficking. It focuses on improving the government&apos;s capacity to support victims, especially women and children, by providing health services, safe housing and educational tools, through a coordinated and strengthened approach. Key actions include developing manuals for health professionals, creating safe spaces for survivors, and forming local committees to combat trafficking. The initiative also involves training government officials and establishing educational tools to prevent trafficking, particularly in schools&#x200b;. IOM will provide technical assistance to the Ecuadorian Government, for the development of tools, guidelines, and manuals, and also leads the implementation of various activities in order to improve safe spaces for trafficking survivors. Furthermore, IOM will promote prevention through education, working closely with the Ministry of Education, and helped develop tools such as the &quot;Caja de Juegos&quot;, always ensuring and evaluating the projects&#xb4; sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
